# ─── Obsidian ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-machine UI state — ignoring these prevents merge conflicts when the same
# vault is opened on more than one device. Shared config (app.json,
# core-plugins.json, community-plugins.json, appearance.json, graph.json,
# templates.json, daily-notes.json) IS tracked on purpose.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.trash/

# Plugin code — reinstall per device from Obsidian's community plugin browser.
# community-plugins.json (the list of what to install) stays tracked.
.obsidian/plugins/

# Kept even though the line above already covers it: if plugin code is ever
# committed for version parity, this must STILL never be committed — plugins
# store access tokens in their data.json.
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# ─── Credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.pat
.git-credentials

# ─── Camera originals & editing sidecars ───────────────────────────────────
# This vault is for *knowledge*, not for storage of negatives. RAW files are
# 20-60 MB each and will blow past GitHub's limits fast. Keep originals in your
# normal photo library / cloud backup and put only small web-sized JPEGs in
# attachments/ as visual references.
*.CR2
*.CR3
*.NEF
*.NRW
*.ARW
*.SRF
*.SR2
*.RAF
*.ORF
*.RW2
*.PEF
*.DNG
*.3FR
*.IIQ
*.xmp

# Editor working files (large, binary, not diffable)
*.psd
*.psb
*.tif
*.tiff
*.lrcat
*.lrcat-*
*.lrdata/
*.lrprev
*.co
*.cof
*.coprof
*.capture1
*.dop
*.on1
Adobe Bridge Cache*
.CaptureOne/

# Video
*.mov
*.mp4
*.mts
*.m4v
*.avi

# ─── OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
